      "content": "That data is helpful for the report. To round this out, can you elaborate a bit more on the \"recovery time\" aspect? \n\nWhen a major disruption occurs—say, a vehicle breaks down in the middle of the intersection or a pedestrian makes an unexpected crossing—what does the actual breakdown of the system look like in terms of how the flow stabilizes? I'm trying to understand if the \"chaos\" or \"friction\" in these scenarios follows a predictable pattern or if it's just completely random interference.",
